  - contextual articulation
  - acquisition
  - artificial general intelligence
repository-code: "https://github.com/mnespace/mnespace"
abstract: >-
  Generative Memory Theory (GMT) proposes that the substance guiding
  intelligent behavior is generative memory rather than stored knowledge.
  Meta-space is the functional setting in which an agent continually
  constructs an associative memory structure from interaction with digital
  and physical environments, organized to guide perception, imagination,
  and action. The paper presents a functional model M = (G, F), the
  activation-selection-expression pipeline, construction dynamics
  (sedimentation, calibration, restructuring), contextual articulation,
  acquisition, eight falsifiable propositions with matched-control
  experiments, a reference architecture, and an evaluation design. The AGI
  claim is a necessity hypothesis, not a sufficiency claim.
